Domain idea: gotocm.io


Tasks can be simply Go structures. Compileable by Go. Good start.
Or a special language, but then compiled before sending.
Requires task writer to have Go installation anyway.


Idempotent tasks.

Allow dry-run mode.
Allow dry-run-only permission for specific user/machine (like, production).

Every task must be able to run in dry-run mode. 
What about raw scripts?


Very fast state gathering.
Btw using ansible's "facts gathering" term is so confusing,
because of the artificial difference between os-wide facts
and task-scoped state.


`blockinfile` equivalent - here I want to use sth like block_regexp
option so that we really can substitute a block in one pass.


Provide "diff-control" not only for template but for all file-modifying
tasks - line: lineinfile, blockinfile ..etc.


Ansible's static/dynamic include mess - don't copy that.


By default work around Linux inconsistencies
(like, service names: ntp/ntpd, ssh/sshd, apache2/httpd
